# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values from your Supabase
# project settings (Project Settings > API). Do not commit `.env.local`.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# RLS integration-test fixtures (src/lib/supabase/rls.integration.test.ts).
# Credentials for three permanent, pre-seeded throwaway accounts (two plain
# users + one admin) used only to exercise Row Level Security policies
# against the real hosted project. Optional: when unset, the integration
# suite skips cleanly instead of failing.
#
# NEVER fill these in with a real user's email/password -- these accounts
# (one of them an admin) live in the same project as real data, so their
# credentials are as sensitive as any other admin login.
RT_TEST_USER_A_EMAIL=
RT_TEST_USER_A_PASSWORD=
RT_TEST_USER_B_EMAIL=
RT_TEST_USER_B_PASSWORD=
RT_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL=
RT_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Shared secret for the public /refer teacher-referral form (Phase 3, Part
# B). Checked both by the Server Action (this var -- server-only, no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, must never reach the client bundle) and independently
# inside the database by submit_teacher_referral(), against a hash stored in
# app_config. Generate a strong random value, e.g.:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
# and seed the matching value into app_config.teacher_referral_secret_hash
# (hashed with pgcrypto's crypt()/gen_salt('bf'), never stored in plaintext).
TEACHER_REFERRAL_SECRET=

# Outgoing app email (welcome emails, pairing notifications -- see
# src/lib/email/send.ts). Server-only, no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Sent via
# Gmail SMTP + nodemailer with an app password: use a Google account with
# 2-Step Verification enabled, then create an App Password at
# https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords and paste it here (not the
# account's normal login password). If unset, sends are skipped with a
# console.warn instead of failing the action that triggered them.
#
# Note: this is separate from Supabase's own auth emails (signup
# confirmation, password reset) -- those are sent by Supabase itself, and
# its built-in mailer only delivers to project team members. To have real
# users receive those, configure custom SMTP in the Supabase dashboard
# (Auth > SMTP) with these same GMAIL_USER / GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD credentials.
GMAIL_USER=
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=
